WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:01.860
- I know someone's gonna enjoy that,

00:00:01.860 --> 00:00:03.900
but I don't get to enjoy that.

00:00:03.900 --> 00:00:05.480
It's officially 2020
(party horn blowing)

00:00:05.480 --> 00:00:07.070
and a new year is upon us,

00:00:07.070 --> 00:00:08.770
so everybody's looking to try out

00:00:08.770 --> 00:00:10.620
a new diet, a new challenge,

00:00:10.620 --> 00:00:13.950
and I did exactly that for
the last 30 days with Whole30.

00:00:13.950 --> 00:00:17.060
No added sugar, no grains,
no legumes, no dairy,

00:00:17.060 --> 00:00:20.410
no alcohol, no measurements,
no MSG or sulfites,

00:00:20.410 --> 00:00:23.670
and no fake junk food
with approved ingredients.

00:00:23.670 --> 00:00:24.990
It's really a short list,

00:00:24.990 --> 00:00:27.430
but if you really dive
in a look at the rules,

00:00:27.430 --> 00:00:31.270
each one technically
eliminates whole food groups.

00:00:31.270 --> 00:00:33.185
And boy, was it a challenge for me.

00:00:38.718 --> 00:00:40.958
The original plan was to start Whole30

00:00:40.958 --> 00:00:44.628
immediately after my birthday,
which falls on November 12th.

00:00:44.628 --> 00:00:45.898
Just turned 30, by the way,

00:00:45.898 --> 00:00:48.328
and that was a big occasion to celebrate.

00:00:48.328 --> 00:00:50.558
So I don't wanna be following
any restrictive diets

00:00:50.558 --> 00:00:51.758
in that moment, you know what I'm sayin'?

00:00:51.758 --> 00:00:53.288
A little sweets never hurt nobody.

00:00:53.288 --> 00:00:54.498
Cookies and cream milkshake!

00:00:54.498 --> 00:00:58.465
But then, I began having
some serious second thoughts.

00:00:58.465 --> 00:01:00.235
(police siren wailing)

00:01:00.235 --> 00:01:01.763
But Doctor Mike, you always said

00:01:01.763 --> 00:01:03.788
elimination diets are no good!

00:01:03.788 --> 00:01:05.418
They can fuel eating disorders

00:01:05.418 --> 00:01:08.318
and even nutritional
deficiencies at times.

00:01:08.318 --> 00:01:11.598
And now you're gonna do it
yourself and endorse it?

00:01:11.598 --> 00:01:12.448
No!

00:01:12.448 --> 00:01:14.731
This is not an endorsement.

00:01:16.345 --> 00:01:17.761
This is.

00:01:17.761 --> 00:01:22.148
This is not an endorsement
of Whole30 for everybody.

00:01:22.148 --> 00:01:24.308
It's not a universal recommendation.

00:01:24.308 --> 00:01:27.228
In fact, there are very few
universal recommendations

00:01:27.228 --> 00:01:29.138
that doctors give to their patients.

00:01:29.138 --> 00:01:31.528
Whole30 is something I wanted to try.

00:01:31.528 --> 00:01:33.878
I wanted to see how my
body responded to it.

00:01:33.878 --> 00:01:35.338
If you want a video talking about

00:01:35.338 --> 00:01:38.808
the true pros and cons from the
scientific angle of Whole30,

00:01:38.808 --> 00:01:40.175
that's linked down below.

00:01:40.175 --> 00:01:42.675
(light music)

00:01:43.548 --> 00:01:46.928
The rules of Whole30, a lot
of them make sense to me,

00:01:46.928 --> 00:01:49.298
and I was fine following them.

00:01:49.298 --> 00:01:51.038
But there were a few that I knew

00:01:51.038 --> 00:01:53.378
were gonna be problematic
right off the bat,

00:01:53.378 --> 00:01:56.508
and those two are no grains and no dairy.

00:01:56.508 --> 00:01:57.718
I can cut out bread.

00:01:57.718 --> 00:01:59.468
That's not a problem,
I've done that before

00:01:59.468 --> 00:02:01.438
when I was gluten sensitive in the past.

00:02:01.438 --> 00:02:02.928
I've overcome that.

00:02:02.928 --> 00:02:06.488
But the fact that I have to
give up brown rice, quinoa,

00:02:06.488 --> 00:02:09.318
things that I eat, part of a healthy diet.

00:02:09.318 --> 00:02:11.748
My sushi, that's, you know what I eat,

00:02:11.748 --> 00:02:13.098
that's like my go-to meal,

00:02:13.098 --> 00:02:15.808
so I was gonna be suffering
without having rice.

00:02:15.808 --> 00:02:17.868
And then to not have cheese?

00:02:17.868 --> 00:02:20.618
Cheese, cheese, it's what
makes the world go round.

00:02:20.618 --> 00:02:23.188
It's like my favorite
thing, even in salads,

00:02:23.188 --> 00:02:25.118
you need to put a little
blue cheese crumble in there

00:02:25.118 --> 00:02:26.358
to make it taste good.

00:02:26.358 --> 00:02:29.078
So I knew right away that
that was gonna be a problem.

00:02:29.078 --> 00:02:32.378
What I tried to do was to plan
a little bit more thoroughly.

00:02:32.378 --> 00:02:35.168
Figure out what places I can still eat in,

00:02:35.168 --> 00:02:38.188
but just make sure that my food
was still Whole30 approved.

00:02:38.188 --> 00:02:40.108
For example, on a work day.

00:02:40.108 --> 00:02:44.568
All right, my usual midday
work meal is Chipotle.

00:02:44.568 --> 00:02:47.258
And I initially thought I
couldn't have Chipotle on Whole30,

00:02:47.258 --> 00:02:48.348
but boy, was I wrong.

00:02:48.348 --> 00:02:50.288
All I had to do was take
out the rice and beans,

00:02:50.288 --> 00:02:51.121
and I'm good to go.

00:02:51.121 --> 00:02:53.538
Oh, and the cheese
obviously, I love cheese.

00:02:53.538 --> 00:02:55.008
So what do I have in my bowl?

00:02:55.008 --> 00:02:58.658
Salad bowl, double the meat
chicken, mild salsa, guacamole,

00:02:58.658 --> 00:03:00.738
and the fajita vegetables.

00:03:00.738 --> 00:03:02.423
Sounds yummy!

00:03:02.423 --> 00:03:04.923
(light music)

00:03:05.788 --> 00:03:08.838
Boy, did I make a mistake giving up sweets

00:03:08.838 --> 00:03:11.798
during the sweetest time of the year!

00:03:11.798 --> 00:03:14.295
Oh, I'm trying to start
my first day of Whole30,

00:03:14.295 --> 00:03:16.098
and then what is this?

00:03:16.098 --> 00:03:18.648
What is this?

00:03:18.648 --> 00:03:21.888
And then, what is this?
(woman laughing)

00:03:21.888 --> 00:03:23.618
It's ridiculous in here!

00:03:23.618 --> 00:03:26.428
Holidays, birthdays, retirements.

00:03:26.428 --> 00:03:29.668
There were cakes and
chocolate bars everywhere!

00:03:29.668 --> 00:03:32.158
Part of trying to give something up,

00:03:32.158 --> 00:03:35.118
your success depends on
getting away from those things.

00:03:35.118 --> 00:03:37.458
I made sure that I didn't
have any sweets in my house

00:03:37.458 --> 00:03:38.348
so I couldn't cheat.

00:03:38.348 --> 00:03:42.918
But constantly being met with
sweets galore in the hospital,

00:03:42.918 --> 00:03:44.568
that was a serious challenge for me,

00:03:44.568 --> 00:03:46.418
and I was like, "Oh my
God, am I gonna give in?"

00:03:46.418 --> 00:03:48.858
But for some reason having those rules

00:03:48.858 --> 00:03:50.088
made it a little bit easier,

00:03:50.088 --> 00:03:51.948
because I just deferred to the rules.

00:03:51.948 --> 00:03:54.522
As opposed to like, "No,
I really shouldn't."

00:03:54.522 --> 00:03:57.022
(light music)

00:03:57.978 --> 00:04:00.518
Boy, I missed something big.

00:04:00.518 --> 00:04:03.538
What holiday falls from
the middle of November

00:04:03.538 --> 00:04:04.688
to the middle of December?

00:04:04.688 --> 00:04:05.878
Thanksgiving.

00:04:05.878 --> 00:04:07.328
How'd I not think this through?

00:04:07.328 --> 00:04:09.288
And on top of it, I was invited

00:04:09.288 --> 00:04:12.748
to an amazing Thanksgiving Greek dinner.

00:04:12.748 --> 00:04:16.060
And if you've never had a
Greek dinner. (lips smooching)

00:04:16.060 --> 00:04:19.232
The Whole30 struggle is real
at a Greek Thanksgiving.

00:04:19.232 --> 00:04:20.911
Do you agree?

00:04:20.911 --> 00:04:21.918
- Oh yeah.
- It's not like my

00:04:21.918 --> 00:04:23.178
sous-vide cooking days,

00:04:23.178 --> 00:04:25.528
so not too long ago, it's
much, much better than that.

00:04:25.528 --> 00:04:27.438
Basically, all I could put on my plate

00:04:27.438 --> 00:04:29.468
was the turkey and some peas.

00:04:29.468 --> 00:04:31.378
'Cause anything else had cheese on it

00:04:31.378 --> 00:04:32.648
or some kind of grain,

00:04:32.648 --> 00:04:34.198
and I was just sitting there unhappily.

00:04:34.198 --> 00:04:35.908
Everyone looked at me like I was crazy.

00:04:35.908 --> 00:04:38.060
You know that scene from
"My Big Fat Greek Wedding"?

00:04:38.060 --> 00:04:40.574
- What do you mean he don't eat no meat?

00:04:40.574 --> 00:04:42.275
- "What do you mean you don't eat no rice?

00:04:42.275 --> 00:04:43.628
"Oh, it's okay, we have cake!"

00:04:43.628 --> 00:04:44.461
I'm like, "No!"

00:04:44.461 --> 00:04:47.436
Do you know how bad I
wanna eat this right now?

00:04:47.436 --> 00:04:49.936
(light music)

00:04:50.888 --> 00:04:53.818
One of the rules of Whole30 is
that you can't drink alcohol.

00:04:53.818 --> 00:04:56.558
To me, not a big deal,
not a bing drinker anyway.

00:04:56.558 --> 00:04:58.948
I'll have a glass of wine
or a drink here and there

00:04:58.948 --> 00:05:00.328
for celebratory purposes.

00:05:00.328 --> 00:05:04.138
But now, I went to Miami for Art Basel.

00:05:04.138 --> 00:05:05.698
If you don't know what Art Basel is,

00:05:05.698 --> 00:05:07.808
it's like a fancy-schmancy art event

00:05:07.808 --> 00:05:10.198
where it's a ton of exhibits in Miami.

00:05:10.198 --> 00:05:13.248
Great weather, great
people, everyone's happy,

00:05:13.248 --> 00:05:14.318
people are having drinks.

00:05:14.318 --> 00:05:15.298
If you've never been to Miami,

00:05:15.298 --> 00:05:17.508
a big part of the
celebrations during Art Basel

00:05:17.508 --> 00:05:18.598
is to go out at night.

00:05:18.598 --> 00:05:21.098
I've never really gone out to night clubs

00:05:21.098 --> 00:05:23.228
without having at least one drink.

00:05:23.228 --> 00:05:24.191
It's not about getting drunk for me.

00:05:24.191 --> 00:05:27.148
It's just about, you know,
having a drink and loosening up.

00:05:27.148 --> 00:05:30.788
But being out with 2 Chainz
on top of you singing,

00:05:30.788 --> 00:05:32.768
and I'm there just drinking water,

00:05:32.768 --> 00:05:35.535
everyone felt like I was
a buzzkill at this thing.

00:05:35.535 --> 00:05:36.905
"Mike, have a drink with us," you know,

00:05:36.905 --> 00:05:38.998
"Cheers, cheers, cheers," and
I would be cheersing water,

00:05:38.998 --> 00:05:40.218
and people would get offended.

00:05:40.218 --> 00:05:41.818
I was able to withstand that.

00:05:41.818 --> 00:05:42.948
But I could easily see

00:05:42.948 --> 00:05:45.068
how if you're trying to follow Whole30,

00:05:45.068 --> 00:05:48.537
the peer pressure can really
motivate someone to cheat.

00:05:48.537 --> 00:05:51.037
(light music)

00:05:51.958 --> 00:05:53.638
I was movin', I was groovin',

00:05:53.638 --> 00:05:55.458
I was startin' to feel good on Whole30.

00:05:55.458 --> 00:05:57.685
I was even getting proud
telling people like,

00:05:57.685 --> 00:06:00.388
"Oh no, no rice for me, just sashimi."

00:06:00.388 --> 00:06:02.138
Or whatever it is I was eating.

00:06:02.138 --> 00:06:03.488
But then disaster struck.

00:06:03.488 --> 00:06:05.508
Again, probably due to poor planning,

00:06:05.508 --> 00:06:06.838
but it was a true disaster.

00:06:06.838 --> 00:06:08.328
Went to the gym a few times,

00:06:08.328 --> 00:06:11.918
and my bench started going
down, which makes no sense.

00:06:11.918 --> 00:06:16.503
Normally, when I'm working out,
I'm benching like 225, 255.

00:06:16.503 --> 00:06:19.228
225 was becoming a huge challenge for me.

00:06:19.228 --> 00:06:21.108
When I stepped onto the basketball court,

00:06:21.108 --> 00:06:23.848
after one game, I felt
like I was exhausted.

00:06:23.848 --> 00:06:25.008
It made no sense to me.

00:06:25.008 --> 00:06:26.898
It's not because I turned 30!

00:06:26.898 --> 00:06:29.158
It's probably because I was
undereating my calories.

00:06:29.158 --> 00:06:31.718
When you do an elimination
diet like Whole30,

00:06:31.718 --> 00:06:33.538
it's very easy to under eat calories.

00:06:33.538 --> 00:06:35.608
This is probably why a
lot of people lose weight.

00:06:35.608 --> 00:06:37.498
But now myself being an athlete,

00:06:37.498 --> 00:06:40.968
I needed to plan for that, I
should have thought more ahead.

00:06:40.968 --> 00:06:43.595
To make sure that I can still perform

00:06:43.595 --> 00:06:46.339
(imitates net swishing) on
the court and in the gym, bah!

00:06:46.339 --> 00:06:48.839
(light music)

00:06:49.678 --> 00:06:53.158
Once I threw in some extra
calories, things improved a lot.

00:06:53.158 --> 00:06:55.898
I was having less cravings,
performing better in the gym.

00:06:55.898 --> 00:06:57.458
Actually, my body probably looked the best

00:06:57.458 --> 00:07:00.308
that it's looked in
some time following this

00:07:00.308 --> 00:07:03.828
because I did a lot of caloric
restriction, unintentionally,

00:07:03.828 --> 00:07:07.168
and then kept working out,
and then up my protein.

00:07:07.168 --> 00:07:08.568
Just got back from the gym,

00:07:08.568 --> 00:07:11.268
so I need my little post workout meal.

00:07:11.268 --> 00:07:14.188
Whole30 approved, we got Wild Planet,

00:07:14.188 --> 00:07:16.048
a little grilled chicken,
oops, I spilled some.

00:07:16.048 --> 00:07:18.998
I was even already so
used to the eating habits,

00:07:18.998 --> 00:07:20.798
like of things I could and couldn't eat,

00:07:20.798 --> 00:07:22.438
then when I would go out
to eat with somebody,

00:07:22.438 --> 00:07:24.858
they would get an awesome little bun cake,

00:07:24.858 --> 00:07:27.558
or some rice, something
that looks delicious.

00:07:27.558 --> 00:07:29.468
I wasn't even stressing it anymore.

00:07:29.468 --> 00:07:32.308
Once you get out of old habits,
and you develop new ones,

00:07:32.308 --> 00:07:33.298
it's not that big of a deal.

00:07:33.298 --> 00:07:35.658
I was actually feeling really
good and proud of myself

00:07:35.658 --> 00:07:37.183
that I was getting to the end.

00:07:37.183 --> 00:07:39.683
(light music)

00:07:40.598 --> 00:07:43.118
Now when you hit your
30-day mark, it's not over.

00:07:43.118 --> 00:07:47.318
You then enter the phase of
reintroduction of the foods

00:07:47.318 --> 00:07:51.118
one by one to see how they
would affect your body.

00:07:51.118 --> 00:07:52.398
Because the whole premise of this

00:07:52.398 --> 00:07:55.538
is not only to develop a
better relationship with foods,

00:07:55.538 --> 00:07:57.308
but it's also to see if those foods

00:07:57.308 --> 00:07:58.598
negatively affect your body.

00:07:58.598 --> 00:08:00.248
It's just like the claim of Whole30

00:08:00.248 --> 00:08:03.188
that I'm not a huge fan of,
it's not really scientific.

00:08:03.188 --> 00:08:06.758
Like if you put in
legumes on the first day,

00:08:06.758 --> 00:08:08.548
then two days later, added sugars,

00:08:08.548 --> 00:08:12.688
then two days after that,
grains, it's not scientific.

00:08:12.688 --> 00:08:15.218
If we're doing a proper
elimination challenge

00:08:15.218 --> 00:08:18.748
in the medical setting, we
do a 90-day elimination.

00:08:18.748 --> 00:08:20.948
We keep a strict log of symptoms.

00:08:20.948 --> 00:08:23.718
We then do a reintroduction one at a time

00:08:23.718 --> 00:08:26.278
to see if and when symptoms return.

00:08:26.278 --> 00:08:28.758
I can put in legumes on day one,

00:08:28.758 --> 00:08:30.518
day two, I can put in grains,

00:08:30.518 --> 00:08:32.268
and then have symptoms on day six,

00:08:32.268 --> 00:08:34.248
and it could be due to any one of those.

00:08:34.248 --> 00:08:35.238
It's not very scientific,

00:08:35.238 --> 00:08:36.805
'cause you don't know
what's happening there.

00:08:36.805 --> 00:08:39.305
(light music)

00:08:40.168 --> 00:08:42.478
If you followed my
previous 30-day challenges,

00:08:42.478 --> 00:08:46.178
you know that my digestive
system becomes an absolute mess.

00:08:46.178 --> 00:08:48.128
I mean, bloating, diarrhea.

00:08:48.128 --> 00:08:49.958
Whenever I make any
kind of drastic changes,

00:08:49.958 --> 00:08:52.038
and believe me, this was a drastic change.

00:08:52.038 --> 00:08:54.418
When I began that reintroduction phase,

00:08:54.418 --> 00:08:56.028
everything went back to normal.

00:08:56.028 --> 00:08:58.668
I mean, yes, I included
more vegetables in my diet,

00:08:58.668 --> 00:09:00.675
but by doing so, everything
returned back to normal

00:09:00.675 --> 00:09:02.438
and I started feeling good again.

00:09:02.438 --> 00:09:05.208
I just think that these
major, drastic changes

00:09:05.208 --> 00:09:07.298
when you're already eating healthy

00:09:07.298 --> 00:09:10.068
probably aren't great for your microbiome

00:09:10.068 --> 00:09:11.288
and your overall gut health.

00:09:11.288 --> 00:09:13.738
So I find out when I eat my normal diet

00:09:13.738 --> 00:09:16.328
that's right for my body
and my athletic needs,

00:09:16.328 --> 00:09:19.248
it works best for me,
but with more vegetables.

00:09:19.248 --> 00:09:21.158
Something I noticed was
that I was struggling

00:09:21.158 --> 00:09:23.878
to get my fiber from my meals.

00:09:23.878 --> 00:09:26.448
Because normally, I would
eat things like black beans,

00:09:26.448 --> 00:09:29.788
at least three, four
times a week, brown rice.

00:09:29.788 --> 00:09:31.568
And when I had to eliminate all those,

00:09:31.568 --> 00:09:33.378
I had to find replacement sources.

00:09:33.378 --> 00:09:35.918
And yeah, vegetables, fruits,
there's stuff in there.

00:09:35.918 --> 00:09:37.448
I think if I was to do it again,

00:09:37.448 --> 00:09:39.078
I would probably supplement with something

00:09:39.078 --> 00:09:40.778
just to make sure I get enough fiber.

00:09:40.778 --> 00:09:43.278
(light music)

00:09:44.208 --> 00:09:46.228
One of the main questions people asked me

00:09:46.228 --> 00:09:48.248
when I was almost at the end of Whole30

00:09:48.248 --> 00:09:50.108
was how did my body change?

00:09:50.108 --> 00:09:52.548
Well, I definitely saw some weight loss,

00:09:52.548 --> 00:09:55.298
but remember, part of the
rules are no measurements.

00:09:55.298 --> 00:09:56.628
I didn't weigh myself.

00:09:56.628 --> 00:09:58.028
What I did notice was that my clothes

00:09:58.028 --> 00:09:59.878
were fitting a lot more loose,

00:09:59.878 --> 00:10:01.808
my pants were a little baggier.

00:10:01.808 --> 00:10:05.178
Even my watch started sort
of hanging on my hand.

00:10:05.178 --> 00:10:07.818
Maybe I was losing muscle 'cause
I was undereating calories,

00:10:07.818 --> 00:10:10.508
but there's definitely ways
you can mitigate all of that

00:10:10.508 --> 00:10:12.188
depending on what your goals are.

00:10:12.188 --> 00:10:13.418
That's why my recommendation

00:10:13.418 --> 00:10:15.298
is to never just do these on a whim.

00:10:15.298 --> 00:10:17.798
Talk to a nutritionist,
a registered dietician,

00:10:17.798 --> 00:10:20.478
a physician, somebody that
can give you some guidance

00:10:20.478 --> 00:10:21.558
on what you should be doing.

00:10:21.558 --> 00:10:24.468
In fact, my whole gripe with Whole30

00:10:24.468 --> 00:10:27.848
is that it really encourages
people to do this on a whim.

00:10:27.848 --> 00:10:29.565
They're like, "Oh, if you're fatigued,

00:10:29.565 --> 00:10:31.148
"try this, it may help."

00:10:31.148 --> 00:10:32.758
It's true, it may help,

00:10:32.758 --> 00:10:34.478
especially if you're
eating a ton of junk food.

00:10:34.478 --> 00:10:36.848
But what if you have
a vitamin D deficiency

00:10:36.848 --> 00:10:38.158
that you're not aware of,

00:10:38.158 --> 00:10:40.598
and then you do Whole30,
you don't eat dairy,

00:10:40.598 --> 00:10:42.938
and that worsens your
vitamin D deficiency.

00:10:42.938 --> 00:10:44.228
Or you're anemic or something.

00:10:44.228 --> 00:10:45.928
I mean, there's so many reasons

00:10:45.928 --> 00:10:47.448
why people can have symptoms.

00:10:47.448 --> 00:10:49.978
That's exactly the reason
why you should be evaluated

00:10:49.978 --> 00:10:52.968
before you start a drastic
elimination diet like this.

00:10:52.968 --> 00:10:55.768
That's not knocking Whole30,
that's just spitting facts.

00:10:55.768 --> 00:10:56.908
At the end of the day,

00:10:56.908 --> 00:10:59.968
nutritional advice
should be individualized,

00:10:59.968 --> 00:11:02.288
but it's a very restrictive diet,

00:11:02.288 --> 00:11:04.258
it can cause some serious problems.

00:11:04.258 --> 00:11:06.008
There's definitely some research showing

00:11:06.008 --> 00:11:08.678
that there's some crossover
with eating disorders,

00:11:08.678 --> 00:11:10.748
and most the time, it's unnecessary.

00:11:10.748 --> 00:11:12.678
I just feel that there's other ways

00:11:12.678 --> 00:11:14.278
of getting someone to eat healthy

00:11:14.278 --> 00:11:17.558
than to give them a strict
list of eight things to do.

00:11:17.558 --> 00:11:19.268
And eliminating some foods

00:11:19.268 --> 00:11:21.008
that I think are otherwise healthy.

00:11:21.008 --> 00:11:23.568
Why would you eliminate
certain foods like black beans

00:11:23.568 --> 00:11:26.518
that can be so healthy to
the majority of people?

00:11:26.518 --> 00:11:27.818
A lot of it doesn't make sense.

00:11:27.818 --> 00:11:30.118
But look, if you want a
challenge for yourself,

00:11:30.118 --> 00:11:32.538
like I did, and you
wanna do it the safe way,

00:11:32.538 --> 00:11:35.028
make sure you talk to a
nutritionist or a doctor,

00:11:36.609 --> 00:11:38.749
If you wanna see my
other 30-day challenges

00:11:38.749 --> 00:11:41.709
and a green tea video, click
on this playlist right here.

00:11:41.709 --> 00:11:44.209
(light music)

